Introduction of Cypress?
1. Frontend web based automation testing tool.
2. Its tool to test Modern Web based Application (New frameworks such as reactJS, Angular JS uses to WebSites).
3. Cypress capable to automate any application which runs over browser.
4. In Cypress we write test scripts by using javascripts and TypeScript.
5. Cypress doesnot uses any selenium library, its completely different from selenium.
6. Cypress is an opensources 
	1. Cypress Runner - opensources (up to 80% of automation task can be done at runner, writing,  
	   running, custom function etc.)
	2. Cypress dashboard - testcases maintained, parallel execution. comes with paid version.
7. Cypress run on nodejs environment (similiar like selenium runs on java (JDK/JRE))

Who, can use cypress? - both dev and QA can use.
1. Initally dev team uses Cypress to perform unit and integration testing.
2. Later QA starts using it
3. E2E - Testcases
4. API Testing.

Difference with selenium and Cypress

Main Feature of Cypress.
1. Time Travel --> capture screenshot of each steps
2. Automatic Wait.
3. Consistence (Flaky test in selenium webdriver).
4. screenshot and video part is avaialbe in cypress.
5. cross browser testing.


Limitations of Cypress.
1. cannot automate desktop based application
2. limitated browser supports
3. supports available for javascripts and type scripts
4. reading and writing data from external files is difficult.
5. Third party integration supports is not there.(reporting)

